      "path": "/books/al-kafi:1:4:59:6",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّ الْإِمَامَ يَعْرِفُ الْإِمَامَ الَّذِي مِنْ بَعْدِهِ فَيُوصِي إِلَيْهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Idrees, from Muhammad Bin Abdul Jabbar, from Safwan Bin Yahya, from Ibn Abu Usman, from Al Moalla Bin Khunays, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The Imam<sup>asws</sup> recognises the one who is to be (the Imam<sup>asws</sup>) after him<sup>asws</sup>, so he<sup>asws</sup> bequeaths to him<sup>asws</sup>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 6. Ahmad ibn Idris has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Jabbar from Safwan ibn Yahya from (ibn) abu ‘Uthman from al-Mu‘alla ibn Khunays from abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.) who has said the following “The Imam (a.s.) knows the succeeding Imam and delivers his will to him.”"
        ]
      }
    },
